    "notes": "Compiled 2026-11-20 from a Claude Research pass (notes/tools/llm-landscape/recherche-2026-11.json), transformed by notes/dev/build-landscape.mjs. SCALE: AA Intelligence Index v5.0.1, where the top Claude (Fable 5.2, max effort) scores 65. v5 (2026-10-27) replaced v4.3.2 with a new set of nine evaluations, mostly agentic and long-horizon; open-weight models fell much further than closed ones and low scorers were compressed toward zero, so this file is NOT comparable with earlier snapshots, only rankings within it are. AA reports v5 scores for eight open models (Qwen3.8-27B, Nanbeige4.3-33B, Muse Glimmer, Nemotron 3.5 Super VL and Lightning, gpt-oss-120b, Gemma 4 31B, Mistral Small 4); every other score is mapped from v4.3.2 by a curve fitted to those pairs and marked score_estimated, Gemma 4 shifted down 1.5 points because its 31B fell further than the curve. Most pre-2026 models now sit at 0 to 2 and are not separable. Scores are highest-effort; lower reasoning effort scores lower. New this snapshot: Nanbeige4.3-33B, plus the Claude Fable 5.2 anchor; every model of the previous snapshot is carried forward. Known source conflicts are kept as widened bands rather than resolved. Architecture blocks restored from the verified previous snapshot because this pass only estimated them: Qwen3.6-27B, Qwen3.5-27B, Gemma 4 12B, Muse Glimmer 30B, Mistral Medium 3.5 (128B), Mistral Small 4 (119B-A6B). Corrected against the published config.json: Nanbeige4.3-33B. Models too large for the biggest preset (120 GB usable) even at Q3_K_M were dropped for the fit view: none."
